  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8800;0</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a complex number. Then, the set of all complex numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;satisfying the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>w</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, for some real number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mo></math>,&nbsp;is"
  },
